description:
Objective: CQ-I06 DoD 2. A packaged plugin must contain every production helper asset it needs, and no test artifacts. Three defects were verified on 2026-10-30:
(a) packages/moe-proxy/tsconfig.json compiles src/*.test.ts. Its dist/ therefore holds index.test.js, input-framing.test.js, utils.test.js and workerType.test.js, with their .d.ts and .map files. Both bundlers copy that dist wholesale: moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts through from(bundledProxyDir), and moe-vscode/scripts/bundle-assets.mjs.
(b) The daemon build compiles the test-only src/tools/toolTestHarness.ts into dist/tools/toolTestHarness.js, and both plugins ship it. Only *.test.ts files import it.
(c) Both IDEs' Managed VM panels (CQ-I03, CQ-I05) spawn scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs. It ships only because the bundlers copy local-runner/**: no bundler required-list, onboarding check or bundle test names it.

Deliverable:
- packages/moe-daemon/tsconfig.json excludes src/tools/toolTestHarness.ts.
- Both bundlers add vm-control.mjs to their required local-runner assets, and drop **/*.test.* and **/*.spec.* from the daemon and proxy dist copies.
- scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs, in its packaged-bundle block, does three things:
  - requires local-runner/vm-control.mjs;
  - runs the packaged vm-control.mjs with no arguments and asserts exit 2 and exactly {"code":"VM_CONTROL_INPUT_INVALID"}. That proves its whole static import closure loads from the bundle, without touching Multipass, the ledger or the daemon;
  - fails on any test artifact under the bundle's daemon/, proxy/ or scripts/, excluding node_modules.
- scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs covers all of it.

Out of scope:
- the proxy tsconfig, which keeps typechecking proxy tests at build;
- what the npm-published moe-proxy package contains;
- node_modules dev dependencies;
- ci.yml and docs, which belong to CQ-I06;
- any runtime behaviour change.

Verification (run fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs

implementationPlan.description:
MINIMUM IMPLEMENTATION, four files. Keep each file's existing LF and UTF-8 encoding, and report every file.

1. packages/moe-daemon/tsconfig.json: `"exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/tools/toolTestHarness.ts"]`. Only *.test.ts files import the harness; grep shows no production importer. So dist stops shipping a test fixture and nothing at runtime changes.
2. moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts:
   - add "vm-control.mjs" to requireBundledAssets' local-runner listOf(...);
   - in prepareSandbox, add `exclude("**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*")` inside BOTH `from(bundledDaemonDir) { ... }` and `from(bundledProxyDir) { ... }`, with a one-line comment: moe-proxy's tsconfig compiles src/*.test.ts, and compiled tests never ship.
   - Do not touch the node_modules, scripts or docs copies.
3. moe-vscode/scripts/bundle-assets.mjs:
   - add 'vm-control.mjs' to the required local-runner list;
   - give copyDir an `excludeTests` option. Its filter rejects a file whose path.basename matches /\.(test|spec)\./. Pass it only for `copyDir(asset.dist, distOut, { excludeTests: true })`;
   - keep the excludeBin semantics for deps unchanged.
4. scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs: inside `if (bundle) { ... }` and BEFORE the `const require = createRequire(proxyEntry);` boundary, because the bundle test slices up to it:
   - Add 'local-runner/vm-control.mjs' to the bundled-file list.
   - Run the packaged producer with no arguments: `spawnSync(process.execPath, [path.join(bundle, 'scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs')], { encoding: 'utf8', windowsHide: true, timeout: 30_000 })`. Add spawnSync to the existing child_process import.
     - assert status === 2, with a message naming vm-control and quoting stderr;
     - assert stdout === '{"code":"VM_CONTROL_INPUT_INVALID"}\n'.
     - Usage validation happens before any read, so nothing touches Multipass, the ledger or the daemon. ESM loads the whole static import closure first, so a pass proves the closure.
   - Scan for test artifacts. A small recursive readdirSync(withFileTypes) walk over the bundle's daemon/, proxy/ and scripts/:
     - skip any directory named node_modules;
     - flag a directory named tests, __tests__, fixtures, __fixtures__, __e2e__ or __acceptance__;
     - flag a file whose name matches /\.(test|spec)\.|testharness/i;
     - collect '/'-joined relative paths, and finish with `assert.deepEqual(found, [], 'Bundled test artifact(s): ' + found.join(', '))`.

Error handling: every refusal is an assert that fails the run with an exact, path-naming message. The scan never follows node_modules, and a missing top-level directory is reported rather than skipped silently.

Run the step 1 file again: all of it must pass, including the existing tests. Then run node scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs's existing unbundled mode only if dist builds exist; that is optional here.
